{"data": [{"author_id": "1992461", "conversation_id": "2118437296567472419", "created_at": "2026-11-06T00:52:12.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118506704031957403"], "id": "2118506704031957403", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 37, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@scaling01 ECI is Anthropic's own internal scale, so \"4 AECI ≈ 3 months of frontier progress\" only holds inside that ruler. Without a shared external benchmark, the 178.6 is a self-graded score, not a cross-lab comparison.", "url": "https://x.com/fishjar/status/2118506704031957403"}, {"author_id": "1382053851323326466", "conversation_id": "2118437296567472419", "created_at": "2026-11-06T00:23:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118499453229502823"], "id": "2118499453229502823", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 166, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@scaling01 Any estimates on OpenAI's internal model", "url": "https://x.com/Christo31306687/status/2118499453229502823"}, {"author_id": "1206226124641951744", "conversation_id": "2118437296567472419", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:54:43.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118477138181685747"], "id": "2118477138181685747", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 375, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@scaling01 1/ either benchmark is false\n2/ the model disclosed isn't the same as the one they're training to release in the future, might just be an internal checkpoint they give out internally or something like that\n\n3/ fallbacks. It's fallback to a lower level model on few tasks (refusing", "url": "https://x.com/YashasGunderia/status/2118477138181685747"}, {"author_id": "1466416677713854477", "conversation_id": "2118437296567472419", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:27:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118470222139044288"], "id": "2118470222139044288", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 670, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@scaling01 That also explains why they are so far ahead of the competition", "url": "https://x.com/Laz01L/status/2118470222139044288"}, {"author_id": "1868615832009375744", "conversation_id": "2118437296567472419", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:05:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118464661716652476"], "id": "2118464661716652476", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 670, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@scaling01 My question is, where does Fable 5.5 fit in then? Between Opus 5.5 and Model 4?", "url": "https://x.com/veluminemusic/status/2118464661716652476"}, {"author_id": "1245489368548151303", "conversation_id": "2118437296567472419", "created_at": "2026-11-05T21:48:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118460361414197474"], "id": "2118460361414197474", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 643, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@scaling01 Isn't per year AECI progress ~29 now? So about 1.5 months. Which tracks?", "url": "https://x.com/bunny_albino/status/2118460361414197474"}, {"author_id": "1756786321534631936", "conversation_id": "2118437296567472419", "created_at": "2026-11-05T21:25:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118454594447823134"], "id": "2118454594447823134", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 136, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@wenhaocha1 @scaling01 I would say probably new pretrain. We heard about model 2 in august. I find it very unlikely, that they just spend the time posttraining that model.", "url": "https://x.com/Johanne61545102/status/2118454594447823134"}, {"author_id": "1483945570595127298", "conversation_id": "2118437296567472419", "created_at": "2026-11-05T21:11:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118451153906102402"], "id": "2118451153906102402", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1332, "like_count": 6, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@scaling01 any idea model 2/3/4 are pretrain or just posttrain?", "url": "https://x.com/wenhaocha1/status/2118451153906102402"}, {"author_id": "2103432423300046848", "conversation_id": "2118437296567472419", "created_at": "2026-11-05T20:51:05.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118446024041841077"], "id": "2118446024041841077", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 158, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@scaling01 Four months of frontier progress just to increase the cost per million tokens and add another layer of vendor lock-in. Wake me up when open weights catch up to the cost curve.", "url": "https://x.com/CodetocashAi/status/2118446024041841077"}, {"author_id": "1551262560648712192", "conversation_id": "2118437296567472419", "created_at": "2026-11-05T20:50:58.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118445994635575434"], "id": "2118445994635575434", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 716, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@scaling01 Three months of frontier progress, and it finished training before most of us finished evaluating Opus 5.5.", "url": "https://x.com/karanjagtiani04/status/2118445994635575434"}, {"author_id": "1665675488604434434", "conversation_id": "2118437296567472419", "created_at": "2026-11-05T20:33:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118441505937412543"], "id": "2118441505937412543", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1198, "like_count": 4, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@scaling01 nice to see actual dates on this for once", "url": "https://x.com/amybuildsAI/status/2118441505937412543"}, {"author_i